      "problem": "Which of the following shows the point $D(-5,4)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $D.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-5,$ so we move $5$ units to the *left*, in the negative direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $D$ has a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units *up*, in the positive direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14200823/assets/19520b88504572a892e70dc3a40d16a3635c8528f9e591ac82aa0411d8091129.png)",
